TYNDARUS:
(aside.)
Capital! I wouldn’t purchase, at a talent’s price even, Thales the Milesian;

HEGIO:
(to the SLAVES, who obey.)
Release him now forthwith;

HEGIO:
(to PHILOCRATES.)
Follow me, that I may give you your expenses for the journey at my banker’s;

HEGIO:
(aside.)
I’ faith, I compassed my design, when I purchased these men of the Quaestors out of the spoil. I have released my son from slavery, if so it pleases the Gods;
